; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Pixel Art Grid
; CATEGORY: Lists & Data Structures
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     mdarray, grid, arrays, pixel art, colors
; SUMMARY:  Stores a little picture in a two dimensional array of color numbers and paints it square by square.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Pictures on a screen are grids of tiny colored squares. Here the
;   grid is an MDARRAY with 10 rows and 10 columns. Each box holds a
;   color number. The picture starts as rows of digits, the program
;   copies them into the array, then paints the array, then paints a
;   mirror image next to it by reading the columns backward.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. To make your own picture, change the rows in
;   the variable called rows. 0 is black, 4 red, 6 yellow, 7 white.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * MDARRAY [rows columns] makes a grid
;   * MDSETITEM and MDITEM use a [row column] list as the address
;   * nested FOR loops visit every cell
;   * a word like 0440 is also a list of characters you can ITEM
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Draw your initials or a space invader.
;   * Make the squares smaller and the grid bigger.
;   * Paint the picture upside down by counting rows backward.
; ============================================================

; Each row is a word of digits. 9 means "leave empty" so the background
; shows through.
make "rows [
  9994499449
  9944444444
  9444744444
  9444444444
  9444444444
  9944444449
  9994444499
  9999444999
  9999949999
  9999999999
]

make "size 10
make "grid mdarray (list :size :size)

; Copy the digits into the array. ITEM :c of a word gives one digit.
to loadgrid
  for [r 1 10] [
    for [c 1 10] [
      mdsetitem (list :r :c) :grid item :c item :r :rows
    ]
  ]
end

; Paint one square with its top left corner at (x, y).
to pixel :x :y :color
  if :color = 9 [stop]
  penup setxy :x :y setheading 90
  filled :color [repeat 4 [fd 24 rt 90]]
end

; MIRROR = true reads each row from the right end, which flips it.
to paint :left :mirror
  for [r 1 10] [
    for [c 1 10] [
      localmake "col ifelse :mirror [11 - :c] [:c]
      pixel :left + 24 * (:c - 1) 150 - 24 * (:r - 1) mditem (list :r :col) :grid
    ]
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [230 240 255]
loadgrid
paint -300 "false
paint 60 "true
penup setxy -300 -150 setpencolor "black
label [The grid, and the same grid read backward]
print sentence [Color in row 3, column 4 is] mditem [3 4] :grid
